-Grimm-G-072-001"/><edm:isShownBy rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/loris/fmb/fmb-ms-Grimm-G-072-001/fmb-ms-Grimm-G-072-001_002r.jp2/full/full/0/default.jpg"/><edm:object rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/loris/fmb/fmb-ms-Grimm-G-072-001/fmb-ms-Grimm-G-072-001_002r.jp2/full/full/0/default.jpg"/><edm:provider rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/organization/1482250000004671163"></edm:provider><edm:rights rdf:resource="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/3.0/"/></ore:Aggregation><ore:Proxy rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/proxy/europeana/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_ms_Grimm_G_072_001"><dc:date rdf:resource="#1810"></dc:date><dcterms:medium rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/concept/2090"></dcterms:medium><edm:europeanaProxy>true</edm:europeanaProxy><ore:proxyFor rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_ms_Grimm_G_072_001"/><ore:proxyIn rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/europeana/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_ms_Grimm_G_072_001"/><edm:type>TEXT</edm:type></ore:Proxy><ore:Proxy rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/proxy/provider/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_ms_Grimm_G_072_001"><dc:creator>Grimm, Jacob</dc:creator><dc:creator>Grimm, Wilhelm</dc:creator><dc:date>[1810]</dc:date><dc:description>On October 25th and December 15th of 1810, Jacob Grimm sent Clemens Brentano this manuscript. It is the oldest handwritten version of the Kinder- und Hausmärchen since the Brothers Grimm systematically destroyed all the preliminary work for their edition of the fairy tales, probably in order to prevent the comparison between the handwritten versions and the later printed edition (first edition 1812), which was thoroughly revised and expressed in literary form. According to an analysis by Heinz Rölleke (Rölleke Heinz (ed.), Die älteste Märchensammlung der Brüder Grimm. Synopse der handschriftlichen Urfassung von 1810 und der Erstdrucke von 1812, Cologny-Genève 1975), 25 fairy tales were written by Jacob Grimm, 14 by Wilhelm Grimm (partly with addenda by his brother), and 7 can be attributed to four other authors. Martin Bodmer purchased this manuscript from Mary A. Benjamin, New York, in 1953.</dc:description><dc:format>66 ff., 22 x 18 cm</dc:format><dc:identifier>doi:10.5076/e-codices-fmb-ms-Grimm-G-072-001</dc:identifier><dc:identifier>http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/fmb/ms-Grimm-G-072-001</dc:identifier><dc:identifier>Cologny, Fondation Martin Bodmer, G-72.1</dc:identifier><dc:publisher>e-codices - Virtual Manuscript Library of Switzerland</dc:publisher><dc:language>German</dc:language><dc:rights>e-codices / Cologny, Fondation Martin Bodmer (cf. http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/about/terms)</dc:rights><dc:source rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/fmb/ms-Grimm-G-072-001"></dc:source><dc:title>Cologny, Fondation Martin Bodmer, G-72.1 : Grimm, Jacob and Wilhelm, composite manuscript with 45 fairy tales and one saga (autograph, unsigned)</dc:title><dc:type>Autograph</dc:type><dcterms:medium>Paper</dcterms:medium><edm:europeanaProxy>false</edm:europeanaProxy><ore:proxyFor rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_ms_Grimm_G_072_001"/><ore:proxyIn rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/provider/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_ms_Grimm_G_072_001"/><edm:type>TEXT</edm:type></ore:Proxy><edm:EuropeanaAggregation rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/europeana/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_ms_Grimm_G_072_001"><edm:aggregatedCHO rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_ms_Grimm_G_072_001"/><edm:datasetName>9200211_Ag_EU_e-Codices</edm:datasetName><edm:country>Switzerland</edm:country><edm:preview rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/loris/fmb/fmb-ms-Grimm-G-072-001/fmb-ms-Grimm-G-072-001_002r.jp2/full/full/0/default.jpg"/><edm:landingPage rdf:resource="https://www.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_fmb_ms_Grimm_G_072_001"/><edm:language>mul</edm:language><edm:rights rdf:resource="http://cre